<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bad Reichenhall</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bad Reichenhall is a spa town in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, near the Austrian border. Its brine springs were worked from prehistoric times, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its salt was a main source of wealth for the Bavarian dukes and the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>, carried along salt roads across southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Salt is still produced there today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bad-reichenhall.jpg" alt="Bad Reichenhall" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luitold · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:REI_Rathausplatz-1_07.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
